# Correspondence with users. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC: these files carry real names and
# email addresses, and were untracked-but-unignored, i.e. one `git add -A` away from
# being published (the R135 trap, previously hit with MISTAKES.md).
emails/

# --- secret shapes (added 2026-08-24 after R455) ---------------------------------
# A live USPTO API key reached a PUBLIC repo because .uspto_key was documented as
# "gitignored" and never actually added here. .env* was covered; nothing else was.
# These patterns are about SHAPE, not about the one file that leaked: the next secret
# will have a name nobody predicted, so ignore the shapes secrets normally take.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*_key
.*_key
credentials*
*secret*
*.token
token.txt

# local D1 scan-budget counter (volatile, machine-local)
.claude/hooks/.d1_budget.json

# reliability-system session state (machine-local receipts)
.claude/state/

# Internal operational docs - never in the public tree (2026-08-31, see R531)
.claude/
